{
  "name": "Sine-Gordon kinks and breathers",
  "description": "Sine-Gordon field: u has a vacuum at every multiple of 2π, and walls between neighbouring vacua are kinks. Discs at u = 2π are rings of kink; they collapse, bounce, and leave breathers (localized lumps that keep oscillating) plus radiation. The interior is conservative (no friction): radiation shed by the collapsing bubbles would circle the wrap-around field forever, so a sponge border (gamma ramping up over the outer ~28 px) soaks it up, as an infinite domain would let it escape. A small viscosity nu damps only grid-scale ripples; set nu = 0 for purely reversible dynamics. Paint gamma to add or remove absorbers.",
